PyDoc_STRVAR(__pyx_doc_20A03_Ash_Prompt_Vault_16ash_prompt_vault_2_is_child_of_wildcard, "v1.0.2 (B) REWRITE - JSON-aware wildcard-child detection.\n    v1.3.0: SHORT-TEMPLATE SKELETON CHECK added (step 3b).\n\n    LEGACY DEFECTS (the \"clubbed sister images\" bug):\n      1. Any prompt containing \"{\" / \"}\" returned True immediately -\n         every JSON prompt qualified as a wildcard child.\n      2. Similarity was scored on RAW text - JSON boilerplate (keys,\n         braces, commas) dominates, so unrelated JSON prompts scored\n         high against any template.\n      3. record()\047s fallback scan takes the first match over the\n         newest-first wildcard list, so the newest wildcard absorbed\n         every JSON prompt -> unrelated images grouped as sisters.\n\n    ALGORITHM (Cases 1-4 from the vault rules):\n      1. Both sides are reduced to COMPARABLE TEXT: JSON -> the string\n         values only; plain text passes through unchanged (the working\n         non-JSON path, Case C, is preserved).\n      2. The unresolved-slot check runs on comparable text only (JSON\n         structural braces no longer count as wildcard syntax).\n      3. PRIMARY: literal-segment containment - the template is split\n         on its wildcard slots (incl. bare [token] slots, v1.2.0) and\n         the child matches when >= threshold of the template\047s literal\n         text (by length) is present in the child.\n      3b. v1.3.0 SKELETON CHECK (slot-dominated templates, < 40 literal\n         chars): the child must be RESOLVED (no raw slot tokens),\n         COMPLETE (every literal word present) and PROPORTIONATE\n         (word count within the slot-resolution band).\n      4. FALLBACK: word-overlap / SequenceMatcher similarity on\n         comparable text at the raised threshold (0.7).");
